ub:ubus: bugfix for QEMU'addr 8byte check

driver inclusion
category: bugfix
bugzilla: https://atomgit.com/openeuler/kernel/issues/6695
CVE: NA

-----------------------------------------------------------

The address of the task_src variable is 4-byte aligned.
After the address is forcibly converted to an 8-byte
address and then transferred to the assign_bit
interface, the QEMU simulation platform strictly
verifies the 8-byte alignment. As a result, a panic
occurs when the ubus driver is loaded.

Fixes: 5b429f1fd821 ("ub:ubus: Add control software restart features")

