ub:hisi-ubus: modify return value of hi_feature_get() in abnormal branch

driver inclusion
category: bugfix
bugzilla: https://atomgit.com/openeuler/kernel/issues/6695
CVE: NA

-----------------------------------------------------------

hi_feature_get() returns 64 bits feature bitmap, each bit represents a
feature. Bit value 1 means feature enabled, 0 means feature disabled. In
the case feature_sets data is not initialized, we don't want return all
0 directly which means no feature is enabled because this changes the
default behavior(all features are enabled by default). Modify return value
of hi_feature_get() in abnormal branches to U64_MAX meaning all features
are supported by default.

