ub:ubus: modify ub virt notify

driver inclusion
category: bugfix
bugzilla: https://atomgit.com/openeuler/kernel/issues/6695
CVE: NA

-----------------------------------------------------------

When the insmod ubase thread is performing UE probe and the retry
task thread in the VDM is performing MUE probe, the two threads
are executed concurrently.
As a result, the ubase null pointer occurs. The ub_virt_notify
implementation is modified. The return value is checked.
If the MUE driver is not ready or the notification fails
during UE probe, the system retries the probe and does
not continue to execute the subsequent probe process of the UE.

Fixes: 9039065cf6d0 ("ub:ubus: Adding a ue Creation Destruction Mechanism")

ub:ubus: Resolve the link change message is not reported before sending notify message

driver inclusion
category: bugfix
bugzilla: https://atomgit.com/openeuler/kernel/issues/6695
CVE: NA

-----------------------------------------------------------

The link change message is used to obtain the corresponding uent
based on the EID. In the management and control plane scenario,
the management and control process modifies the eid.
If the link change message is delivered before the notify message
is delivered, the uent cannot be obtained based on the EID.
Therefore, in this scenario, the uent can be directly obtained
based on the UBC.

Fixes: 95aa040fe0e7 ("ub:ubus: Support handle device link up and link down")

ub:ubus: Optimize the initialization performance of USI INT_TYPE2

driver inclusion
category: bugfix
bugzilla: https://atomgit.com/openeuler/kernel/issues/6695
CVE: NA

-----------------------------------------------------------

Currently, when initializing interrupt type 2, during the preparation
of each MSI descriptor, access to the device configuration space is
initiated to obtain the number of interrupt vectors and the number
of address tables. This results in repeated accesses many times when
a large number of vectors are requested, which is a redundant action.
Now, it has been optimized to read the values once outside the loop
and then pass them in for direct use.

Fixes: 47b1d5f03a59 ("ub:ubus: Add UBUS MSI basic functions")

ub:ubus: Always invalidate tlb during decoder unmap

